# Expected sha256 of the jetstack Helm chart archives, as written by
#   helm pull jetstack/<chart> --version <version>     (https://charts.jetstack.io)
# in `sha256sum -c` format: "<64 lower-case hex>  <archive file name>", one line
# per archive. The names follow CERT_MANAGER_VERSION and TRUST_MANAGER_VERSION;
# a version bump changes the name and needs a new digest in the same commit.
#
# scripts/istio/install-mesh.sh pulls both archives, checks them against these
# lines (sha256sum -c) and installs from the verified local files only.
# scripts/ci/validate-jetstack-charts.sh (run by validate-manifests.sh in CI)
# verifies them the same way before helm template; a mismatch fails CI.
#
# PLACEHOLDER - NOT A DIGEST. The session that added this file could not reach
# charts.jetstack.io, quay.io/jetstack (OCI) or a GitHub release asset, so it
# could not hash the published archives. Until an operator replaces both
# PLACEHOLDER values, install-mesh.sh --apply fails closed. CI still pulls,
# renders and validates the charts, passes with a warning and prints each
# archive's sha256 as a line "CHART_DIGEST <archive> <sha256>" in the
# validate-manifests log.
#
# To fill: take the CHART_DIGEST lines from a CI run (or the platform thread's
# reading of it) and confirm them with a second, independent pull on a trusted
# network (different machine or network) - both must agree:
#   helm repo add jetstack https://charts.jetstack.io --force-update
#   helm pull jetstack/cert-manager --version v1.19.6 -d ./charts
#   helm pull jetstack/trust-manager --version v0.20.3 -d ./charts
#   (cd ./charts && sha256sum cert-manager-v1.19.6.tgz trust-manager-v0.20.3.tgz)
# then replace the two lines below and record both pulls in the PR.
PLACEHOLDER  cert-manager-v1.19.6.tgz
PLACEHOLDER  trust-manager-v0.20.3.tgz
